## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Conceptual understanding of integration)
## KEYWORDS('definite integral', 'geometric')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLT(IntAreaGraph)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.2')
## Problem1('13')

#Problem APEX 5.2.13

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'plots.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);
Context('Numeric');

$a = 3 * random(1, 8) * 3 + 1;
$b = random(2, 6);

$f1 = Compute("x^2");

$c  = random(1, 5);
$c1 = $c;
$c2 = 2 + $c;

$plot = Plot(
    xmin            => -0.1,
    xmax            =>  2.1,
    xtick_delta     =>  1,
    xminor          =>  0,
    ymin            => -0.25,
    ymax            =>  4,
    ytick_delta     =>  1,
    yminor          =>  0,
    rounded_corners => 1
);
$plot->add_function($f1, 'x', -10, 10, color => 'blue');
$plot->add_dataset([ 1, 0 ], [ 1, 1 ], color => 'blue', width => 1);
$plot->add_dataset([ 2, 0 ], [ 2, 4 ], color => 'blue', width => 1);
$plot->add_label(
    [ 0.75, 0.25, '\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)' ],
    [ 1.5,  0.5,  '\\(\\frac{7}{3}\\)' ]
);

$a8 = Real(8 * $a);

$ans1 = $a8 / 3;
$ans2 = Real(8 / 3 + 2 * $b);
$ans3 = Real(8 / 3);
$ans4 = $ans2;

$alttext = qq~A graph of x^2 with the region under the curve from x=0 to x=1
is given by 1/3 and the region under the curve from x=1 to 2 is given by 7/3.~;

BEGIN_PGML
>>[! [$alttext]!]{$plot}{400} <<

A graph of [`f(x) = x^2`] is shown above.   The numbers shown represent
the geometric area of each region.
Evaluate the following definite integrals.

a) [``\int_0^{2} [$a] x^2 \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans1}{20}

b) [``\int_{0}^{2} (x^2 + [$b]) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans2}{20}

c) [``\int_{[$c1]}^{[$c2]} (x - [$c])^2 \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans3}{20}

d) [``\int_{[$c1]}^{[$c2]} \left((x - [$c])^2 + [$b]\right) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans4}{20}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First note that
[``
  \int_0^2 x^2 \, dx = \int_0^1 x^2 \, dx + \int_1^2 x^2 \, dx =
  \dfrac{1}{3} + \dfrac{7}{3} = \dfrac{8}{3}.
``]

a) 
[``
  \int_0^{2} [$a] x^2 \, dx = 
  [$a] \int_0^{2} x^2 \, dx = [$a]\left( \dfrac{8}{3} \right) = \dfrac{[$a8]}{3}.
``]

b) The area represented is the previous area together with the
area of a rectangle of base 2 and height [$b] (see the graph).
[``
  \int_{0}^{2} (x^2 + [$b]) \, dx = \dfrac{8}{3} + (2)([$b]).
``]

c) The integrand is just a horizontal shift of the original
graph.  
[``
  \int_{[$c1]}^{[$c2]} (x - [$c])^2 \, dx = 
  \int_{0}^{2} x^2 \, dx = \dfrac{8}{3}.
``]

d) This integrand is shifted up and right compared to
[`y = x^2`].
[``
  \int_{[$c1]}^{[$c2]} \left((x - [$c])^2 + [$b]\right)\, dx = 
  \int_{0}^{2} (x^2 + [$b]) \, dx = \dfrac{8}{3} + (2)([$b]).
``]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    

